From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Declare the assertion-only helper of hashed_sort.cpp inline

hashed_sort.cpp defines a static helper that only an assertion calls (ExpectedChunkCount),
so -Wunused-function flags it in a release build. It is declared inline,
which -Wunused-function does not flag and which changes no behavior.

Carried here until upstream takes it; not proposed upstream yet.

---
diff --git a/src/duckdb/src/common/sort/hashed_sort.cpp b/src/duckdb/src/common/sort/hashed_sort.cpp
--- a/src/duckdb/src/common/sort/hashed_sort.cpp
+++ b/src/duckdb/src/common/sort/hashed_sort.cpp
@@ -511,7 +511,7 @@ static void BuildDirectColumnData(ClientContext &client, const vector<LogicalTyp
 	}
 }
 
-static idx_t ExpectedChunkCount(idx_t count) {
+static inline idx_t ExpectedChunkCount(idx_t count) {
 	return (count + STANDARD_VECTOR_SIZE - 1) / STANDARD_VECTOR_SIZE;
 }
 
